    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds **ADR-044: Border Radius**. **Documentation only.** Implementation (3 commits, ~300 lines) lands in a follow-up PR.\n\n**First cycle in this arc with measurable delta across multiple element types.** Search field completes (border from ADR-040 + radius from ADR-044), 135 buttons, 715 inline code pills, message boxes.\n\n## Measurement (Wikipedia CSS, 2026-10-28)\n\n### Value forms — trivially scoped\n\n| Form | Count |\n|---|---|\n| Single value (`2px`) | **10** |\n| `inherit` | 1 |\n| Percentage (`50%`) | 2 |\n| Two / three / four value | **0** |\n| Elliptical (`5px / 10px`) | **0** |\n\n**Zero multi-value and zero elliptical means the v1 grammar is trivial** — parse one length, emit to all four corners.\n\n### First-viewport targets\n\n| Element | HTML count | First char | Predicted delta |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `code` (inline) | **715** | 3648 | Rounded code pills |\n| `.cdx-button` | **135** | 10901 | Rounded buttons |\n| `.cdx-search-input` | 8 | 16008 | **Search field completes** (border 040 + radius 044) |\n| `.cdx-text-input` | 10 | 16177 | Rounded input wrappers |\n| `.cdx-message` | — | issue box | Rounded message box |\n\n**4+ first-viewport changes.** Largest visible delta of the 040-044 arc.\n\n## Scope\n\n### Commit 1 (parse + layout, behavior-neutral)\n- `LayoutBox` gains `border_radius[4]` (TL, TR, BR, BL)\n- `border-radius` shorthand: single value → all four corners\n- Per-corner longhands (`border-top-left-radius` etc.): override shorthand (1 rule uses them in Wikipedia CSS)\n- Percentage → `parse_length` (may resolve to 0 with documented caveat)\n- `inherit` → 0 (deferred; parent `overflow: hidden` clips child to rounded shape, visually equivalent)\n- Zero paint changes — no visible delta\n\n### Commit 2 (paint, visible)\n- New `rounded_rect_path()` helper using `cairo_arc` + `cairo_close_path`\n- `paint_box` uses it when any `border_radius[i] > 0`\n- **Two-fill approach** for border + background:\n  - Outer path filled with `border_color`\n  - Inner path (inset by border-width) filled with `background_color`\n  - Diff = rounded border following the curve (no `cairo_stroke` needed)\n- **PNG verification gate before merge**\n\n### Commit 3 (docs)\n- ADR-044 → Implemented\n- Post-ADR-044 notes in ADR-040 (search field complete), ADR-043 (box-shadow draw order)\n- README + CHANGELOG\n\n## Deferred (per ADR)\n\n- **Percentage radius** (`.cdx-radio__icon { 50% }`) — radio buttons are `display: none` in JS-off state\n- **`inherit`** (`.cdx-text-input__input`) — parent `overflow: hidden` clips child to parent's rounded shape, equivalent visual\n- **Multi-value shorthand** — 0 uses; if encountered, first token only\n- **Elliptical** — 0 uses\n- **`border-radius` transitions**\n- **Rounded box-shadow** — shadow follows the curve (own ADR)\n\n## Reviewer checklist\n\n- [ ] **Two-fill approach for border** — outer `border_color` fill + inner `background_color` fill = rounded border without `cairo_stroke`. Avoids stroke path-offset complexity and naturally handles per-side border cases. Alternative considered (offset + stroke) rejected for v1. Agree?\n- [ ] **Simple radius clamp** (`r[i] = min(r[i], w/2, h/2)`) not full CSS §5.5 proportional clamping. Wikipedia's 2px on 100px+ boxes never triggers clamping. Full algorithm deferred. Agree?\n- [ ] **`inherit` deferred despite 1 use** — the one case has `overflow: hidden` parent (ADR-039), so clipping provides equivalent visual. Documented deviation. Agree?\n- [ ] **Multi-value shorthand: first token only** — zero uses today; first-token fallback is safer than dropping the rule entirely (avoids total visual regression if site adds multi-value later). Agree?\n- [ ] **PNG verification gates merge** — Commit 2 must show search field, buttons, and code pills rounded; no unintended artifacts.\n\n## Test plan\n\nNo code touched. Post-merge: `cmake --build build && ./build/tests/honeybee_tests` — 551 / 2125 unchanged.\n\n## ADR\n\n`docs/decisions/044-border-radius.md` — status Accepted; implementation in follow-up PR.\n\nRefs #214",
